# Saf ERP design rules

When creating or editing UI in this project:

1. **Read first:** [docs/erp-design-guide.md](../../docs/erp-design-guide.md) — single source of truth for typography, spacing, and components.
2. **Do not** introduce new fonts, hex colours, or TailAdmin `text-title-*` / raw `text-2xl`/`text-3xl` on headings or KPIs.
3. **Use semantic classes:** `erp-h1`, `erp-dash-h1`, `erp-metric-value`, `erp-table`, `erp-input`, `erp-btn-primary`.
4. **Prefer Blade components:** `<x-admin.page-header>`, `<x-report.page>`, `<x-admin.stat-card>`, `<x-admin.form.field>`.
5. **Brand:** Outfit font, `brand-500` purple, cream canvas — no rebrand unless explicitly requested.
6. **UI UX Pro Max / external skills:** If used, treat as review hints only — output must match Saf ERP tokens above, not a generated design system.

